==Trivia==
*He is likely a reference to [[wikipedia:Paul Stanley|Paul Stanley]], who was the guitarist of the world-famous rock band [[wikipedia:Kiss (band)|Kiss]].
**Since [[Kory]] and [[Berserkory]] wield axes, Deathkory's weapon being a guitar may be a reference to how the word ''axe'' can also refer to a musician's particular instrument, especially a rock musician's guitar.
**Deathkory's guitar appears to have three tuning pegs, meaning it's ''technically'' a [[wikipedia:Cigar box guitar|cigar box guitar]], a guitar that has only three strings.
*Deathkory's name is a play on ''deathcore'', an extreme metal subgenre combining elements of death metal and metalcore.
**His Japanese name makes the same pun, but relies on ''core'' and ''koa(la)'' being homophones in Japanese.
*He was technically an event enemy for a short time, as his only appearance at first was in [[Empress' Report 5]].

